WEBVTT

1
00:52:27.074 --> 00:52:30.074
What a coziness. Delightful.

2
00:52:38.074 --> 00:52:39.074
Hallelujah.

3
00:52:41.074 --> 00:52:43.074
God is so good.

4
00:52:45.074 --> 00:52:48.074
Really, we don't even know half of how good He is. Really.

5
00:52:51.074 --> 00:52:56.074
This morning I wanted to, or was allowed to, introduce the collection.

6
00:52:56.074 --> 00:53:00.074
And I had a text and then I started reading, and I just kept reading.

7
00:53:00.074 --> 00:53:04.074
I think, this is so beautiful, I'm just going to read something.

8
00:53:05.074 --> 00:53:09.074
And I would like to read 2 Corinthians 9, verses 6 to 15.

9
00:53:10.074 --> 00:53:14.074
And this is actually an introduction to the collection by Paul,

10
00:53:14.074 --> 00:53:19.074
for a gift they wanted to give to the church in Jerusalem at that time.

11
00:53:19.074 --> 00:53:22.074
Nice that we are also involved in that now.

12
00:53:22.074 --> 00:53:26.074
But it is also for every collection, and the principles that are in this are so wonderful.

13
00:53:26.074 --> 00:53:30.074
And I want, therefore I actually want to read the whole story.

14
00:53:30.074 --> 00:53:36.074
Because he draws out such beautiful things from there, that really have to do with,

15
00:53:36.074 --> 00:53:41.074
everything has to do with bringing it back to worship.

16
00:53:41.074 --> 00:53:42.074
It is so beautiful.

17
00:53:42.074 --> 00:53:49.074
And as we start reading from verse 6, he says, consider this if you want to give.

18
00:53:49.074 --> 00:53:52.074
Someone who sows sparingly will also reap sparingly.

19
00:53:52.074 --> 00:53:55.074
Someone who sows generously will also reap generously.

20
00:53:56.074 --> 00:54:01.074
And everyone must decide for themselves how much they want to give.

21
00:54:01.074 --> 00:54:07.074
And let him give it wholeheartedly, without reluctance or compulsion.

22
00:54:07.074 --> 00:54:11.074
For God loves people who give with a cheerful heart.

23
00:54:11.074 --> 00:54:12.074
How beautiful is this?

24
00:54:12.074 --> 00:54:17.074
And God is able to give you everything abundantly.

25
00:54:17.074 --> 00:54:24.074
And as a result, you will have more than enough in all things at all times.

26
00:54:24.074 --> 00:54:28.074
And thus you can also give generously to others.

27
00:54:28.074 --> 00:54:35.074
That is, as it is written in the books, about someone who lives exactly as God wants.

28
00:54:35.074 --> 00:54:38.074
If you want to know, Psalm 112, verse 9.

29
00:54:38.074 --> 00:54:43.074
And Paul says there, he always gives generously to the poor, he or she.

30
00:54:43.074 --> 00:54:47.074
And he or she will be forever righteous.

31
00:54:47.074 --> 00:54:52.074
This is such a beautiful thing, for this is a characteristic of God.

32
00:54:52.074 --> 00:54:58.074
God gives seed to the sower to sow, but also bread to give.

33
00:54:58.074 --> 00:54:59.074
He also takes care of us.

34
00:54:59.074 --> 00:55:05.074
And just as, just like that, he will give seed to you.

35
00:55:05.074 --> 00:55:09.074
He will even give much more seed.

36
00:55:09.074 --> 00:55:14.074
And he will ensure that there is also a great harvest from your good deeds.

37
00:55:14.074 --> 00:55:20.074
And so you will always have much to be able to give away.

38
00:55:20.074 --> 00:55:26.074
And there, well, here comes the worship, there the people will praise God.

39
00:55:26.074 --> 00:55:32.074
For through this gift you are not only helping the believers or poor believers,

40
00:55:32.074 --> 00:55:37.074
but you are also ensuring that many people will start thanking God.

41
00:55:37.074 --> 00:55:43.074
For because you have clearly shown that you want to help, they praise God.

42
00:55:43.074 --> 00:55:49.074
For they see that you are obedient to the good news of Christ.

43
00:55:49.074 --> 00:55:53.074
They see that you are obedient to the gospel of Christ.

44
00:55:53.074 --> 00:55:58.074
And that you want to share generously with them and with everyone.

45
00:55:58.074 --> 00:56:00.074
This is the heart of God, people.

46
00:56:00.074 --> 00:56:02.074
And they will pray for you.

47
00:56:02.074 --> 00:56:07.074
They would love to thank you themselves, because they see how good God is to you.

48
00:56:07.074 --> 00:56:12.074
Let us praise God for being so kind and so good to us.

49
00:56:12.074 --> 00:56:15.074
There are no words for it.

50
00:56:15.074 --> 00:56:19.074
And I think I won't add anything to that.

51
00:56:19.074 --> 00:56:23.074
I enjoy standing together and immediately thanking God.

52
00:56:23.074 --> 00:56:27.074
Thank you, Lord. There are no words for it.

53
00:56:27.074 --> 00:56:29.074
Lord, for your goodness. There are no words for it.

54
00:56:29.074 --> 00:56:32.074
Lord, we cannot put your goodness into words.

55
00:56:32.074 --> 00:56:36.074
Lord, and I thank you that you have given.

56
00:56:36.074 --> 00:56:39.074
Lord, the heart that you yourself have.

57
00:56:39.074 --> 00:56:41.074
Lord, you have the heart of a sower.

58
00:56:41.074 --> 00:56:46.074
Lord, in your harvest. You sow in your harvest. You sow in your harvest. You sow in your harvest.

59
00:56:46.074 --> 00:56:48.074
Lord, wholeheartedly.

60
00:56:48.074 --> 00:56:50.074
Lord, otherwise we would not all be here.

61
00:56:50.074 --> 00:56:55.074
Lord, you always give generously. You are generous.

62
00:56:56.074 --> 00:56:58.074
Lord, and you care.

63
00:56:58.074 --> 00:57:01.074
Lord, and if we follow your heart, you will care.

64
00:57:01.074 --> 00:57:03.074
So beautiful.

65
00:57:03.074 --> 00:57:06.074
Lord, and then it continues.

66
00:57:08.074 --> 00:57:10.074
Then comes true worship.

67
00:57:10.074 --> 00:57:12.074
True worship.

68
00:57:12.074 --> 00:57:14.074
That follows obedience.

69
00:57:14.074 --> 00:57:17.074
Where Pastor Van Esch just spoke about.

70
00:57:17.074 --> 00:57:19.074
It is about our obedience.

71
00:57:20.074 --> 00:57:24.074
That we respond to the good news.

72
00:57:24.074 --> 00:57:26.074
To the gospel.

73
00:57:26.074 --> 00:57:28.074
The generous gospel.

74
00:57:28.074 --> 00:57:31.074
Which brings abundance and life.

75
00:57:31.074 --> 00:57:33.074
And I pray this out.

76
00:57:33.074 --> 00:57:35.074
I pray this out.

77
00:57:35.074 --> 00:57:37.074
Lord, these few words.

78
00:57:37.074 --> 00:57:38.074
Lord, far too few.

79
00:57:38.074 --> 00:57:40.074
I pray this out. Lord, over your church.

80
00:57:40.074 --> 00:57:43.074
Lord, and you will work it out. In the name of King Jesus.

81
00:57:43.074 --> 00:57:45.074
Amen.

82
00:57:50.074 --> 00:57:52.074
You may sit down.

83
00:57:52.074 --> 00:57:54.074
Am I on? Yes, right?

84
00:58:06.074 --> 00:58:08.074
Good morning everyone.

85
00:58:08.074 --> 00:58:10.074
Is everyone happy?

86
00:58:13.074 --> 00:58:15.074
If you are taking notes.

87
00:58:16.074 --> 00:58:20.074
Then you could give this sermon a title just like I did.

88
00:58:20.074 --> 00:58:23.074
I wrote down this morning.

89
00:58:23.074 --> 00:58:25.074
As a title with big words.

90
00:58:25.074 --> 00:58:27.074
Rejoice.

91
00:58:27.074 --> 00:58:29.074
In big letters.

92
00:58:29.074 --> 00:58:31.074
Rejoice.

93
00:58:31.074 --> 00:58:33.074
With an exclamation mark at the end.

94
00:58:33.074 --> 00:58:35.074
If you want to write down a Dutch title.

95
00:58:35.074 --> 00:58:37.074
Then I have a few more words for you.

96
00:58:37.074 --> 00:58:41.074
Always be joyful in the Lord.

97
00:58:42.074 --> 00:58:44.074
And Paul says.

98
00:58:44.074 --> 00:58:46.074
I repeat.

99
00:58:46.074 --> 00:58:48.074
Always be joyful in the Lord.

100
00:58:48.074 --> 00:58:50.074
If you have your Bible with you.

101
00:58:50.074 --> 00:58:52.074
Come with me.

102
00:58:52.074 --> 00:58:54.074
To the letter to the Philippians.

103
00:58:54.074 --> 00:58:57.074
I love that letter.

104
00:58:57.074 --> 00:58:59.074
Is there anyone else with me?

105
00:58:59.074 --> 00:59:02.074
Who thinks that letter is just a wonderful letter.

106
00:59:02.074 --> 00:59:05.074
You should actually be required to raise your heart together.

107
00:59:05.074 --> 00:59:07.074
Because it is the Bible.

108
00:59:11.074 --> 00:59:13.074
You know, dear church.

109
00:59:13.074 --> 00:59:17.074
Last week I also said at the beginning.

110
00:59:17.074 --> 00:59:25.074
When we are in the month of December in the Advent month.

111
00:59:25.074 --> 00:59:29.074
Then it is really a Christianity thing.

112
00:59:29.074 --> 00:59:31.074
To look forward during the Advent month.

113
00:59:31.074 --> 00:59:33.074
Christians have invented.

114
00:59:33.074 --> 00:59:38.074
To look forward to the coming of Jesus.

115
00:59:39.074 --> 00:59:42.074
Sidenote information.

116
00:59:42.074 --> 00:59:45.074
Jesus was not born on December 25.

117
00:59:45.074 --> 00:59:47.074
Half.

118
00:59:52.074 --> 00:59:54.074
Then Jesus was not born.

119
00:59:54.074 --> 01:00:00.074
But we have made a celebration out of it.

120
01:00:00.074 --> 01:00:04.074
And sometimes I do get questions about that.

121
01:00:04.074 --> 01:00:06.074
How do you see this now.

122
01:00:06.074 --> 01:00:09.074
We can debate about this for a long time.

123
01:00:09.074 --> 01:00:12.074
While enjoying a cup of tea.

124
01:00:12.074 --> 01:00:17.074
But I personally feel this way now.

125
01:00:17.074 --> 01:00:19.074
At this moment in my life.

126
01:00:19.074 --> 01:00:23.074
That I seize every situation to glorify Jesus.

127
01:00:23.074 --> 01:00:28.074
Even if certain things are debatable.

128
01:00:28.074 --> 01:00:32.074
But the Advent month in Christianity.

129
01:00:32.074 --> 01:00:34.074
Is presented as a month.

130
01:00:34.074 --> 01:00:37.074
In which we look forward to the coming of Jesus.

131
01:00:37.074 --> 01:00:42.074
And then there are typical Advent month sermons.

132
01:00:42.074 --> 01:00:43.074
Teaching.

133
01:00:43.074 --> 01:00:49.074
In which we as a church look at the coming of the person Jesus.

134
01:00:49.074 --> 01:00:53.074
It also becomes dark in the world.

135
01:00:53.074 --> 01:00:55.074
Like winter days.

136
01:00:55.074 --> 01:00:57.074
Except if you live in Australia.

137
01:00:57.074 --> 01:00:59.074
But it is winter days.

138
01:00:59.074 --> 01:01:01.074
It is dark.

139
01:01:01.074 --> 01:01:05.074
And then people speak of the coming of the light into the world.

140
01:01:05.074 --> 01:01:07.074
So then we talk about warmth.

141
01:01:07.074 --> 01:01:08.074
Then we talk about peace.

142
01:01:08.074 --> 01:01:10.074
Then we talk about the Prince of Peace.

143
01:01:10.074 --> 01:01:12.074
Wonderful Counselor.

144
01:01:12.074 --> 01:01:15.074
And then a lot is spoken about that.

145
01:01:15.074 --> 01:01:17.074
What I did last week.

146
01:01:17.074 --> 01:01:20.074
Is what I find more important still.

147
01:01:20.074 --> 01:01:23.074
And that is namely to especially in this time.

148
01:01:23.074 --> 01:01:26.074
To talk about the true gospel.

149
01:01:26.074 --> 01:01:30.074
Instead of looking at a romantic story.

150
01:01:30.074 --> 01:01:34.074
It is more important to look at what Jesus truly came to do.

151
01:01:34.074 --> 01:01:36.074
For what Jesus truly came to do.

152
01:01:36.074 --> 01:01:39.074
Was anything but romantic.

153
01:01:39.074 --> 01:01:42.074
Jesus is not the romantic king.

154
01:01:42.074 --> 01:01:43.074
He is the Lord.

155
01:01:43.074 --> 01:01:45.074
He is the King of kings.

156
01:01:45.074 --> 01:01:47.074
And that He is kind to our hearts.

157
01:01:47.074 --> 01:01:49.074
Stands as a fact.

158
01:01:49.074 --> 01:01:51.074
He is so good to you.

159
01:01:51.074 --> 01:01:54.074
That I can recommend to everyone.

160
01:01:54.074 --> 01:01:57.074
Continue with Jesus in your life.

161
01:01:58.074 --> 01:02:00.074
But what he has done.

162
01:02:00.074 --> 01:02:04.074
And the true message is that he died on a cross.

163
01:02:04.074 --> 01:02:06.074
For your and my sin.

164
01:02:06.074 --> 01:02:09.074
He died a bloody death.

165
01:02:09.074 --> 01:02:11.074
He hung naked on a cross.

166
01:02:11.074 --> 01:02:14.074
And his skull was pierced with thorns.

167
01:02:14.074 --> 01:02:16.074
Not those little thorns from here in Europe.

168
01:02:16.074 --> 01:02:18.074
But we are talking about long spikes.

169
01:02:18.074 --> 01:02:21.074
He died a shameful death.

170
01:02:21.074 --> 01:02:25.074
Because your and my sin against God is shameful.

171
01:02:25.074 --> 01:02:28.074
And the shame that he bore.

172
01:02:28.074 --> 01:02:30.074
Was the shame that you had brought to the Father.

173
01:02:30.074 --> 01:02:32.074
Through the blood of Jesus.

174
01:02:32.074 --> 01:02:34.074
We are acquitted of our sin.

175
01:02:34.074 --> 01:02:37.074
Can I get a glorious amen on that.

176
01:02:39.074 --> 01:02:41.074
And what I want to teach today.

177
01:02:41.074 --> 01:02:45.074
Is not that bloody death and his resurrection.

178
01:02:45.074 --> 01:02:48.074
But today I do want to talk.

179
01:02:48.074 --> 01:02:51.074
About the joy that we can have in God.

180
01:02:52.074 --> 01:02:55.074
True happiness in Jesus.

181
01:02:55.074 --> 01:02:58.074
Truly being happy with him.

182
01:02:58.074 --> 01:03:01.074
That you truly know what it means to be a Christian.

183
01:03:01.074 --> 01:03:05.074
I know what it is to live without Jesus.

184
01:03:05.074 --> 01:03:08.074
And I also know what it is to be with him.

185
01:03:08.074 --> 01:03:11.074
And being with him is the true joy.

186
01:03:11.074 --> 01:03:14.074
And being without him is fake joy.

187
01:03:14.074 --> 01:03:19.074
Can I get an amen from someone who has experienced this in their life?

188
01:03:21.074 --> 01:03:23.074
This is not fake joy.

189
01:03:23.074 --> 01:03:27.074
Because that fake joy you can try to fake for a while.

190
01:03:27.074 --> 01:03:30.074
But then you ultimately end up in a dead end street.

191
01:03:30.074 --> 01:03:32.074
Literally.

192
01:03:32.074 --> 01:03:36.074
Ultimately, if you try to be happy without Jesus.

193
01:03:36.074 --> 01:03:39.074
You end up in a dead end street.

194
01:03:39.074 --> 01:03:42.074
And that dead end street is literally dead-ending.

195
01:03:42.074 --> 01:03:45.074
And when you finally think to yourself.

196
01:03:45.074 --> 01:03:47.074
And that is called repentance.

197
01:03:47.074 --> 01:03:52.074
This street does not lead me to joy, life, happiness.

198
01:03:52.074 --> 01:03:54.074
And then you turn around.

199
01:03:54.074 --> 01:03:57.074
And then you come to repentance and walk with Jesus.

200
01:03:57.074 --> 01:04:01.074
Then you realize that it is so much better with him.

201
01:04:01.074 --> 01:04:04.074
Hallelujah. Praise the Lord.

202
01:04:07.074 --> 01:04:10.074
Philippians Chapter 4 please.

203
01:04:12.074 --> 01:04:14.074
Praise God.

204
01:04:15.074 --> 01:04:18.074
Philippians Chapter 4 verse 1 says.

205
01:04:18.074 --> 01:04:21.074
Therefore, make sure brothers and sisters.

206
01:04:21.074 --> 01:04:24.074
That you remain one with the Lord.

207
01:04:24.074 --> 01:04:26.074
I love you, says Paul.

208
01:04:26.074 --> 01:04:32.074
I long to see you again.

209
01:04:32.074 --> 01:04:37.074
I am happy about you and proud of you.

210
01:04:37.074 --> 01:04:40.074
And that is what I want to talk about today.

211
01:04:41.074 --> 01:04:47.074
About how it is quite possible to be happy with God as a church.

212
01:04:47.074 --> 01:04:53.074
And that you may also be appropriately proud of who you are in the name of Jesus.

213
01:04:53.074 --> 01:04:56.074
But you need certain reflections for that.

214
01:04:56.074 --> 01:05:02.074
Together with Paul, you must look at the ingredients that are in your faith.

215
01:05:02.074 --> 01:05:06.074
To be able to say, oh Lord, I am so happy.

216
01:05:06.074 --> 01:05:08.074
I am so happy with you.

217
01:05:08.074 --> 01:05:11.074
And then you can be proud of your faith.

218
01:05:11.074 --> 01:05:17.074
Paul writes different letters to different congregations in the Bible.

219
01:05:17.074 --> 01:05:20.074
And some letters are quite substantial.

220
01:05:20.074 --> 01:05:26.074
Some letters, the Christians really get a good telling off.

221
01:05:26.074 --> 01:05:33.074
So the letter to the Galatians is just a letter with heavy punches.

222
01:05:33.074 --> 01:05:38.074
The letter to the Galatians was meant to really put the Christians in their place.

223
01:05:38.074 --> 01:05:44.074
In the letter to the Galatians, you actually read more about discipline than rewards.

224
01:05:44.074 --> 01:05:48.074
But the letter to the Philippians is a true love letter.

225
01:05:48.074 --> 01:05:54.074
The letter to the Philippians is a letter where Paul says what we have just read.

226
01:05:54.074 --> 01:05:57.074
If you are still looking here, I am proud of you.

227
01:05:57.074 --> 01:06:02.074
And when I was reading this sermon and praying about it beforehand.

228
01:06:02.074 --> 01:06:08.074
I would also say today, church, I am truly proud of Open Church.

229
01:06:08.074 --> 01:06:13.074
I am truly proud of this church. I am proud of us.

230
01:06:13.074 --> 01:06:16.074
But we need to look at what we are proud of.

231
01:06:16.074 --> 01:06:20.074
And how is it that you can be proud of the church?

232
01:06:20.074 --> 01:06:23.074
Of what we are and who we are and what we do.

233
01:06:23.074 --> 01:06:28.074
And that is why I would like to quickly go through the letter to the Philippians with you.

234
01:06:28.074 --> 01:06:35.074
Let's read just a little bit further. Verse 4 says, rejoice always in the Lord.

235
01:06:35.074 --> 01:06:41.074
And Paul then says, and I say it again, rejoice.

236
01:06:41.074 --> 01:06:49.074
In fact, rejoicing in God is a command from the Bible.

237
01:06:49.074 --> 01:06:56.074
Rejoicing in God is not something that is a feeling that just happens to you.

238
01:06:56.074 --> 01:07:02.074
It is not the case that you come to church and sit with your arms crossed waiting.

239
01:07:02.074 --> 01:07:07.074
Or that it might be a match or that you might be able to rejoice.

240
01:07:07.074 --> 01:07:11.074
For it is not in that way that joy always comes upon you.

241
01:07:11.074 --> 01:07:15.074
It is not an emotion that happens to you or not.

242
01:07:15.074 --> 01:07:18.074
Being happy is a choice, church.

243
01:07:19.074 --> 01:07:26.074
Being happy is something you choose for yourself in faith in Jesus.

244
01:07:26.074 --> 01:07:33.074
And that is why Paul says here, always be happy. And I say it again, just be happy, church.

245
01:07:33.074 --> 01:07:39.074
Be happy with who you are. What we just read from Psalm 16.

246
01:07:39.074 --> 01:07:45.074
Verse 5, let all people see that you are kind. The Lord is near you.

247
01:07:45.074 --> 01:07:51.074
Do not worry about anything, but tell God in prayer what you need.

248
01:07:51.074 --> 01:07:58.074
Dear church, I want to encourage us that when we read these verses, you are always in self-reflection.

249
01:07:58.074 --> 01:08:02.074
And that you see this as a conversation between yourself and God. Is that an idea?

250
01:08:02.074 --> 01:08:06.074
So do not worry about anything, church.

251
01:08:06.074 --> 01:08:14.074
But tell God in prayer what you need. Thank Him also for everything.

252
01:08:15.074 --> 01:08:22.074
Then the peace of God, which we cannot possibly understand, will guard your hearts and your thoughts.

253
01:08:22.074 --> 01:08:26.074
In whom? In Jesus Christ.

254
01:08:26.074 --> 01:08:36.074
And brothers and sisters, set your thoughts on everything that is true, honest, holy, kind, beautiful, and good.

255
01:08:36.074 --> 01:08:40.074
Do everything you have learned, seen, and heard from me.

256
01:08:40.074 --> 01:08:43.074
And here it comes, this is Jesus Christ, the Christmas message.

257
01:08:43.074 --> 01:08:48.074
Then the God of peace will be with you.

258
01:08:48.074 --> 01:08:52.074
Then the God of peace will be with you.

259
01:08:52.074 --> 01:08:54.074
What am I proud of?

260
01:08:54.074 --> 01:09:02.074
For when I read this letter, when I read the letter to the Philippians, I am actually reading the letter to Open Church.

261
01:09:02.074 --> 01:09:04.074
I mean this seriously.

262
01:09:04.074 --> 01:09:07.074
I am happy with this church.

263
01:09:08.074 --> 01:09:12.074
I am really so happy with this church. I am happy with you, I am happy with this church.

264
01:09:12.074 --> 01:09:14.074
I am happy with myself.

265
01:09:18.074 --> 01:09:21.074
Why? Because it is a self-reflection.

266
01:09:21.074 --> 01:09:27.074
Sometimes people ask themselves the question, okay, if God were to write a letter to this church,

267
01:09:27.074 --> 01:09:31.074
for example just like in the book of Revelation, what letter would He write?

268
01:09:31.074 --> 01:09:36.074
Would He use the letter to the Laodiceans for Open Church?

269
01:09:36.074 --> 01:09:41.074
Maybe, maybe there are ingredients in there that contain warnings for Open Church.

270
01:09:41.074 --> 01:09:44.074
There are probably things we need to adjust as a church.

271
01:09:44.074 --> 01:09:48.074
But you know what is very good? To build each other up in faith.

272
01:09:48.074 --> 01:09:55.074
It is indeed very good to keep each other engaged with encouragement in faith, alongside the gospel about the blood of Jesus, about what He has done for you and me,

273
01:09:55.074 --> 01:10:02.074
that He died on the cross, to always keep each other busy with encouragement in faith.

274
01:10:02.074 --> 01:10:06.074
For an encouragement in faith ensures that you can continue with it.

275
01:10:06.074 --> 01:10:10.074
Sometimes you need warnings, dear church, and then also listen to a warning,

276
01:10:10.074 --> 01:10:16.074
for through a warning you can come to obedience, through obedience you can come to holiness,

277
01:10:16.074 --> 01:10:19.074
and through holiness you can come to blessing.

278
01:10:19.074 --> 01:10:24.074
But when there is blessing, we must especially be happy with those blessings, amen?

279
01:10:25.074 --> 01:10:31.074
Philippians chapter 1, please. Quickly turn back, three pages back.

280
01:10:31.074 --> 01:10:33.074
Philippians chapter 1.

281
01:10:33.074 --> 01:10:35.074
What am I happy about as a church?

282
01:10:35.074 --> 01:10:40.074
Why was Paul, what we read there in Philippians chapter 4 verse 1,

283
01:10:40.074 --> 01:10:46.074
Paul says, every time I pray for you, I am happy about you and I am proud of you.

284
01:10:46.074 --> 01:10:49.074
And then I ask myself the question, Paul, what are you so proud of?

285
01:10:49.074 --> 01:10:55.074
Maybe I can level myself, maybe I can see if I can recognize that in open church,

286
01:10:55.074 --> 01:10:59.074
so that we can be happy together with the things that God is doing in our midst.

287
01:11:01.074 --> 01:11:03.074
Chapter 1 verse 3.

288
01:11:04.074 --> 01:11:06.074
Chapter 1 verse 3.

289
01:11:06.074 --> 01:11:11.074
Every time I think of you, I thank God.

290
01:11:12.074 --> 01:11:16.074
Whenever I pray for you, I am happy about you.

291
01:11:17.074 --> 01:11:18.074
Chapter 5.

292
01:11:18.074 --> 01:11:27.074
For you have believed the Good News since the first day you heard it and you still believe it.

293
01:11:27.074 --> 01:11:30.074
Here is my question to our church.

294
01:11:30.074 --> 01:11:37.074
And these are serious questions, you may raise your hand, you may engage in conversation with me in this sermon.

295
01:11:37.074 --> 01:11:43.074
Listen, who in 2024 has literally made a choice?

296
01:11:43.074 --> 01:11:47.074
I can point them out, I look around and I am so proud of many people in this church.

297
01:11:47.074 --> 01:11:52.074
But who in this church has made a rational choice with themselves saying, listen,

298
01:11:52.074 --> 01:11:57.074
I want to take steps, real steps in faith together with Jesus.

299
01:11:57.074 --> 01:12:00.074
I want to be a disciple of Jesus, can I see your hand?

300
01:12:02.074 --> 01:12:08.074
Because you know, it is good that I see many hands going up and that you need to think carefully about these questions.

301
01:12:08.074 --> 01:12:15.074
For many people, and Vanessa and I warn about this, many people come to church and sit in the church,

302
01:12:15.074 --> 01:12:23.074
but are not actually engaged in putting their lives on the path with Jesus as a disciple.

303
01:12:23.074 --> 01:12:30.074
And that is why we warn to say, make sure you are not just a seed filler,

304
01:12:30.074 --> 01:12:36.074
that you are not just a seat filler, but make sure you listen to the gospel of Jesus

305
01:12:36.074 --> 01:12:39.074
and that you also truly change your life with Jesus.

306
01:12:39.074 --> 01:12:43.074
For Jesus is not looking for people who listen to the Word of God,

307
01:12:43.074 --> 01:12:47.074
Jesus is looking for people who also put the Word of God into action.

308
01:12:48.074 --> 01:12:57.074
So here I ask the question again, who here in this church has made literal choices in 2024 to say,

309
01:12:57.074 --> 01:12:59.074
I will tackle this together with Jesus?

310
01:13:00.074 --> 01:13:01.074
Show me a few hands.

311
01:13:01.074 --> 01:13:04.074
I love you all, I will also raise my hands.

312
01:13:04.074 --> 01:13:05.074
I love you guys.

313
01:13:05.074 --> 01:13:08.074
This is what you can be proud of.

314
01:13:09.074 --> 01:13:13.074
That you can be glad that you can grow in the name of Jesus.

315
01:13:14.074 --> 01:13:17.074
The self-reflection question I had written down is,

316
01:13:17.074 --> 01:13:24.074
I am glad about your strong faith and your spiritual growth.

317
01:13:25.074 --> 01:13:27.074
1 verse 9, read along with me.

318
01:13:27.074 --> 01:13:28.074
1 verse 9 says,

319
01:13:28.074 --> 01:13:34.074
I pray that your love will continue to grow.

320
01:13:34.074 --> 01:13:37.074
For through that, your wisdom will also grow.

321
01:13:37.074 --> 01:13:43.074
Then you will understand the things of God better and better.

322
01:13:44.074 --> 01:13:48.074
I am glad Lord, I am speaking to Jesus at this moment.

323
01:13:48.074 --> 01:13:52.074
Lord, I am happy with the discipleship in Open Church.

324
01:13:52.074 --> 01:13:54.074
Truly, I am so happy about that.

325
01:13:54.074 --> 01:13:56.074
Truly, I am so happy about that.

326
01:13:56.074 --> 01:14:01.074
I am so glad with the people who come to faith in this church.

327
01:14:01.074 --> 01:14:05.074
I am so glad with the baptism services we have.

328
01:14:05.074 --> 01:14:08.074
I am so glad with the discipleship we have.

329
01:14:08.074 --> 01:14:12.074
I am so glad with young people who are truly building their faith.

330
01:14:12.074 --> 01:14:15.074
In a world that is going completely crazy.

331
01:14:15.074 --> 01:14:18.074
And that we see growth in this church.

332
01:14:18.074 --> 01:14:22.074
And I am not just talking about a growth in the number of people.

333
01:14:22.074 --> 01:14:25.074
Glory hallelujah that we are facing a luxury problem.

334
01:14:25.074 --> 01:14:28.074
That there is currently an overflow of people in the bar.

335
01:14:28.074 --> 01:14:30.074
Because the hall is becoming too small.

336
01:14:30.074 --> 01:14:33.074
But God has never been interested in quantity.

337
01:14:33.074 --> 01:14:35.074
God is the God of quality.

338
01:14:35.074 --> 01:14:38.074
He does not look at a large church.

339
01:14:38.074 --> 01:14:41.074
He is not interested at all in large churches.

340
01:14:41.074 --> 01:14:44.074
On the contrary, if God sees a large dirty church.

341
01:14:44.074 --> 01:14:48.074
Then he prefers to cleanse that church and send half of them home.

342
01:14:48.074 --> 01:14:52.074
So that only small groups remain from large churches.

343
01:14:52.074 --> 01:14:55.074
So that when he can continue with a remnant.

344
01:14:55.074 --> 01:14:58.074
A small group of people can continue who say.

345
01:14:58.074 --> 01:15:01.074
Yes, I want it. I want to follow Jesus.

346
01:15:01.074 --> 01:15:03.074
I want to grow in the name of Jesus.

347
01:15:03.074 --> 01:15:07.074
I want him to fill me. I want my sins to be cleansed from me.

348
01:15:07.074 --> 01:15:10.074
And I want to continue as a disciple of Jesus.

349
01:15:10.074 --> 01:15:12.074
This is what God wants.

350
01:15:12.074 --> 01:15:15.074
If you just don't believe, you should read the Bible.

351
01:15:15.074 --> 01:15:17.074
For God goes throughout the Bible.

352
01:15:17.074 --> 01:15:20.074
God always deals swiftly with large groups of people.

353
01:15:20.074 --> 01:15:22.074
If he does not agree with them.

354
01:15:22.074 --> 01:15:25.074
And then he continues with small groups of people.

355
01:15:25.074 --> 01:15:27.074
And with those small groups of people, he says.

356
01:15:27.074 --> 01:15:30.074
Yes, you understand it. And you have my heart.

357
01:15:30.074 --> 01:15:32.074
And I have your heart.

358
01:15:32.074 --> 01:15:35.074
Jesus who talks about what I spoke about last week.

359
01:15:35.074 --> 01:15:37.074
About his blood.

360
01:15:37.074 --> 01:15:39.074
And he speaks about his blood.

361
01:15:39.074 --> 01:15:41.074
And he says to the people.

362
01:15:41.074 --> 01:15:43.074
Thousands of people came to eat bread.

363
01:15:43.074 --> 01:15:45.074
And to eat fish.

364
01:15:45.074 --> 01:15:48.074
Thousands of people came to witness the miracles of Jesus.

365
01:15:48.074 --> 01:15:50.074
As long as their stomachs were filled.

366
01:15:50.074 --> 01:15:52.074
And then at a certain moment Jesus says.

367
01:15:52.074 --> 01:15:54.074
Yes, but bread and fish is really nice.

368
01:15:54.074 --> 01:15:56.074
But you need to have me.

369
01:15:56.074 --> 01:15:58.074
You need to eat my body.

370
01:15:58.074 --> 01:16:00.074
You need to drink my blood.

371
01:16:00.074 --> 01:16:02.074
And then all those people who came for a megachurch.

372
01:16:02.074 --> 01:16:05.074
For a nice, charismatic sermon.

373
01:16:05.074 --> 01:16:07.074
And who listened and said.

374
01:16:07.074 --> 01:16:09.074
What is he saying now?

375
01:16:09.074 --> 01:16:11.074
Do we have to eat his body?

376
01:16:11.074 --> 01:16:13.074
Do we have to drink his blood?

377
01:16:13.074 --> 01:16:15.074
And then Jesus says again.

378
01:16:15.074 --> 01:16:18.074
Because he is not looking for large numbers.

379
01:16:18.074 --> 01:16:20.074
He is looking for your heart.

380
01:16:20.074 --> 01:16:22.074
And then he says to his own disciples.

381
01:16:22.074 --> 01:16:24.074
Okay, so maybe you shouldn't go either?

382
01:16:24.074 --> 01:16:28.074
Jesus would never be a pastor of a megachurch.

383
01:16:28.074 --> 01:16:30.074
Believe me.

384
01:16:30.074 --> 01:16:32.074
Shouldn't you also go? He says.

385
01:16:32.074 --> 01:16:34.074
And then Peter steps forward.

386
01:16:34.074 --> 01:16:36.074
And he says, Lord, you have words of life.

387
01:16:36.074 --> 01:16:38.074
Where should we go?

388
01:16:40.074 --> 01:16:42.074
And I ask myself this.

389
01:16:42.074 --> 01:16:44.074
When I read the Scripture.

390
01:16:44.074 --> 01:16:46.074
When I wake up this morning.

391
01:16:46.074 --> 01:16:50.074
Am I still reading words of life that nourish me?

392
01:16:50.074 --> 01:16:53.074
Am I reading words that say.

393
01:16:53.074 --> 01:16:56.074
Yes, I want this.

394
01:16:56.074 --> 01:16:58.074
I don't want that stuff.

395
01:16:58.074 --> 01:17:00.074
I don't want those thoughts from the world.

396
01:17:00.074 --> 01:17:02.074
I don't want the philosophy of this world.

397
01:17:02.074 --> 01:17:04.074
I don't want the mess of this world.

398
01:17:04.074 --> 01:17:06.074
I want what is here.

399
01:17:06.074 --> 01:17:08.074
I want this for myself.

400
01:17:08.074 --> 01:17:12.074
Is there anyone in 2024 who feels that way?

401
01:17:12.074 --> 01:17:14.074
I want more.

402
01:17:14.074 --> 01:17:16.074
I want to grow.

403
01:17:16.074 --> 01:17:20.074
I don't want to play Christian on Sunday morning.

404
01:17:20.074 --> 01:17:24.074
I want to be a Christian at 7. At 7 I want to be a Christian.

405
01:17:24.074 --> 01:17:26.074
With ups and downs, church.

406
01:17:26.074 --> 01:17:28.074
With ups and downs.

407
01:17:28.074 --> 01:17:30.074
I hope that Open Church is a church.

408
01:17:30.074 --> 01:17:32.074
Where we can be real with each other.

409
01:17:32.074 --> 01:17:34.074
That if there is mess in your life.

410
01:17:34.074 --> 01:17:36.074
That we can talk to each other.

411
01:17:36.074 --> 01:17:39.074
Because growth is not just about growth.

412
01:17:39.074 --> 01:17:41.074
But also about pruning.

413
01:17:41.074 --> 01:17:44.074
And when there is growth, there is also clutter.

414
01:17:44.074 --> 01:17:46.074
Pruning needs to happen.

415
01:17:46.074 --> 01:17:48.074
But pruning hurts.

416
01:17:48.074 --> 01:17:49.074
And pruning is not pleasant.

417
01:17:49.074 --> 01:17:51.074
And so many churches fall apart.

418
01:17:51.074 --> 01:17:54.074
Because they don't find the concept of pruning interesting.

419
01:17:54.074 --> 01:17:56.074
Because pruning is going back.

420
01:17:56.074 --> 01:17:57.074
And it seems like going back.

421
01:17:57.074 --> 01:17:59.074
But it is precisely for growth.

422
01:17:59.074 --> 01:18:01.074
In the name of Jesus.

423
01:18:01.074 --> 01:18:08.074
Oh people, I can testify like no other how often I have been pruned in my life.

424
01:18:08.074 --> 01:18:11.074
Cutting into the flesh of Tim.

425
01:18:11.074 --> 01:18:12.074
Exposed.

426
01:18:12.074 --> 01:18:13.074
In the light.

427
01:18:13.074 --> 01:18:14.074
Secret brought to light.

428
01:18:14.074 --> 01:18:15.074
Pain brought to light.

429
01:18:15.074 --> 01:18:17.074
Sin brought to light.

430
01:18:17.074 --> 01:18:19.074
Foolish attitudes brought to light.

431
01:18:19.074 --> 01:18:23.074
And every time there is pruning, it hurts.

432
01:18:23.074 --> 01:18:26.074
But when you are pruned in the name of Jesus.

433
01:18:26.074 --> 01:18:30.074
It is through his love that it is not as painful as I had thought.

434
01:18:31.074 --> 01:18:34.074
Oh dear church, let yourself be pruned by Jesus.

435
01:18:34.074 --> 01:18:36.074
Please, please.

436
01:18:36.074 --> 01:18:39.074
Iron sharpens iron, says the Bible.

437
01:18:39.074 --> 01:18:42.074
And when a brother or sister comes to you in this church.

438
01:18:42.074 --> 01:18:48.074
Please let it be someone who is trustworthy and has authority in Jesus.

439
01:18:48.074 --> 01:18:52.074
But when you are pruned by the Word or by a brother or sister.

440
01:18:52.074 --> 01:18:53.074
Don't be offended.

441
01:18:53.074 --> 01:18:55.074
So do not be offended and walk away.

442
01:18:55.074 --> 01:18:56.074
But accept it.

443
01:18:56.074 --> 01:18:58.074
For this is the church that the Lord has given you.

444
01:18:58.074 --> 01:19:01.074
You will have to do it with us.

445
01:19:01.074 --> 01:19:05.074
This is the church where the Lord has placed you.

446
01:19:05.074 --> 01:19:07.074
And I'm happy with it.

447
01:19:07.074 --> 01:19:10.074
I knew that I was going to do a lot of rambling today.

448
01:19:10.074 --> 01:19:15.074
But Paul is addressing his own church in Philippi here.

449
01:19:15.074 --> 01:19:18.074
Yes, that's what it's called.

450
01:19:18.074 --> 01:19:20.074
Spiritual growth.

451
01:19:20.074 --> 01:19:22.074
Ask yourself this question, dear church.

452
01:19:22.074 --> 01:19:24.074
Think carefully.

453
01:19:24.074 --> 01:19:25.074
Self-reflection.

454
01:19:25.074 --> 01:19:29.074
Think about what I just read in verse 3 and in verse 9.

455
01:19:29.074 --> 01:19:34.074
Do I truly believe in the blood of Jesus Christ?

456
01:19:34.074 --> 01:19:36.074
Think carefully.

457
01:19:36.074 --> 01:19:38.074
This is not a shout or a clap moment.

458
01:19:38.074 --> 01:19:40.074
Just think for yourself.

459
01:19:40.074 --> 01:19:42.074
Do I truly believe?

460
01:19:42.074 --> 01:19:45.074
Please, please do yourself a favor.

461
01:19:45.074 --> 01:19:47.074
Do not be hypocritical.

462
01:19:47.074 --> 01:19:49.074
Especially not in your own thoughts.

463
01:19:49.074 --> 01:19:52.074
In your own thoughts, you can be the most honest.

464
01:19:52.074 --> 01:19:55.074
What you say out loud, you can still put on a show about.

465
01:19:55.074 --> 01:19:58.074
But when you think about yourself, at least you are honest.

466
01:19:58.074 --> 01:20:05.074
Do you truly believe in the love offering that Jesus has given for your life?

467
01:20:05.074 --> 01:20:07.074
Do you still really believe in that?

468
01:20:07.074 --> 01:20:12.074
And are you still truly willing to keep growing in that?

469
01:20:12.074 --> 01:20:16.074
To not stop there, but to keep growing.

470
01:20:16.074 --> 01:20:17.074
Falling and rising.

471
01:20:17.074 --> 01:20:19.074
Three steps forward, two steps back.

472
01:20:19.074 --> 01:20:21.074
Three steps forward, one step back.

473
01:20:21.074 --> 01:20:24.074
But we are moving forward in the name of Jesus. Amen?

474
01:20:24.074 --> 01:20:26.074
Reflect on that.

475
01:20:26.074 --> 01:20:32.074
And if you trace within yourself that there is still spiritual growth,

476
01:20:32.074 --> 01:20:34.074
then you may be glad about that.

477
01:20:34.074 --> 01:20:37.074
In Christ. Right?

478
01:20:37.074 --> 01:20:39.074
We never...

479
01:20:39.074 --> 01:20:42.074
But always in the Lord you are glad.

480
01:20:42.074 --> 01:20:47.074
That is why Paul says in Philippians 1:4, always be glad in the Lord.

481
01:20:47.074 --> 01:20:50.074
I repeat, always be joyful in the Lord.

482
01:20:51.074 --> 01:20:55.074
Another question I ask myself for this church,

483
01:20:55.074 --> 01:20:57.074
and I will not mention any names,

484
01:20:57.074 --> 01:21:01.074
because then I might embarrass people

485
01:21:01.074 --> 01:21:05.074
who really do not like to be put in the spotlight.

486
01:21:05.074 --> 01:21:06.074
But here is a question.

487
01:21:06.074 --> 01:21:08.074
For some people, that is,

488
01:21:08.074 --> 01:21:13.074
do I persevere despite difficulties?

489
01:21:14.074 --> 01:21:18.074
Do I persevere despite difficulties?

490
01:21:18.074 --> 01:21:20.074
I could point them out so easily.

491
01:21:20.074 --> 01:21:23.074
And then I could say, I am so proud of you for continuing,

492
01:21:23.074 --> 01:21:24.074
despite difficulties.

493
01:21:24.074 --> 01:21:27.074
And I will not make eye contact, because then you might think,

494
01:21:27.074 --> 01:21:28.074
oh, this one and that one and that one.

495
01:21:28.074 --> 01:21:33.074
But truly, I know so many testimonies in this church of people

496
01:21:33.074 --> 01:21:38.074
who are struggling, who have tough days, who have difficult days.

497
01:21:38.074 --> 01:21:42.074
And then you might say to yourself, when you have difficult days

498
01:21:42.074 --> 01:21:45.074
and you come to a church where everything is happy and clappy

499
01:21:45.074 --> 01:21:50.074
and Jesus heals and Jesus delivers and Jesus blesses and you become rich, rich, rich.

500
01:21:50.074 --> 01:21:54.074
And then you think to yourself, yes, but I am still dealing with this problem.

501
01:21:54.074 --> 01:21:59.074
And then you can become disappointed, while everything that is said about Jesus healing is true,

502
01:21:59.074 --> 01:22:04.074
Jesus forgives, Jesus delivers, Jesus protects, Jesus provides.

503
01:22:04.074 --> 01:22:05.074
It is all true.

504
01:22:05.074 --> 01:22:08.074
